%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ca23d3e41cd5424c9ec72c610ef25a4, type: 3}
  m_Name: HighHrothgar2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  autoFocusSpeaker: 1
  screens:
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267988772749408
    - rid: 4351267988772749409
    - rid: 4351267988772749410
    - rid: 4351267988772749411
    - rid: 4351267988772749412
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 17d7fb6524a48624b8f800e8b355e0ad, type: 2}
    dialog: '-what do you mean by: "how malleable" is the Thu''um?'
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267988772749413
    - rid: 4351267988772749414
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, you taught me the three words of the "Force Unrelenting" shout,
      and got me started on "Whirlwind Sprint."
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 17d7fb6524a48624b8f800e8b355e0ad, type: 2}
    dialog: Yes?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: So, what would happen if I swapped out one of the words of power with
      another one?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 17d7fb6524a48624b8f800e8b355e0ad, type: 2}
    dialog: It wouldn't do anything if you didn't know the true underlying meaning
      of-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: For the sake of argument, I know the true underlying meaning of every
      word of power involved in the swap.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: What would happen?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 17d7fb6524a48624b8f800e8b355e0ad, type: 2}
    dialog: Well...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 17d7fb6524a48624b8f800e8b355e0ad, type: 2}
    dialog: It would depend on the meaning of the words.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: So, as long as I understand the true meanings of each piece, I can string
      together words of power as I see fit?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 17d7fb6524a48624b8f800e8b355e0ad, type: 2}
    dialog: There would likely be detrimental consequences for misspeaking, but-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 17d7fb6524a48624b8f800e8b355e0ad, type: 2}
    dialog: If successful, you would enact your will, your intention.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: To the letter?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 17d7fb6524a48624b8f800e8b355e0ad, type: 2}
    dialog: Again, that would depend on accurate pronunciation and internal comprehension.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I see...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ({mc}, what are you trying to do?)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: (Make a new shout.)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Must shouts be only three words?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 17d7fb6524a48624b8f800e8b355e0ad, type: 2}
    dialog: Not inherently, no...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 17d7fb6524a48624b8f800e8b355e0ad, type: 2}
    dialog: But again, you would need to understand what you are saying.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 17d7fb6524a48624b8f800e8b355e0ad, type: 2}
    dialog: Adding more words of power complicates the message.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I see...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: 'So, do you know the words for: long, distance, and communication?'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (I see what you're trying to do there, {mc}.)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267988772749415
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 17d7fb6524a48624b8f800e8b355e0ad, type: 2}
    dialog: And what do you hope to do with this knowledge?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267988772749416
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I mean, I think's it's kind of obvious I want to speak across vast distances...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 17d7fb6524a48624b8f800e8b355e0ad, type: 2}
    dialog: And what will you say?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, it would depend on the day, but I'd like to be able to tell things
      to my friends, no matter where they are.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I assume you're asking to see if my intentions follow the Way of the
      Voice?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 17d7fb6524a48624b8f800e8b355e0ad, type: 2}
    dialog: ... your mind is quicker than most men we've met.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267988772749417
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, I wouldn't describe Skyrim as a place that incentivizes abstract
      thought, especially since living to see tomorrow is a luxury some cannot afford.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (Is everyone in Skyrim really that dumb?)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: (I wouldn't say that they're dumb, per se...)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: (But the type of game Skyrim tries to be has no place for really deep
      thinking; the gameplay loop doesn't really have the room for that.)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Anyway, while I suppose there are plenty of ways those words could be
      used for personal glory and conquest...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267988772749418
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I doubt Kynareth would consider uplifting others to new ideas, information,
      or perspectives, regardless of location, offensive.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Especially since she seems invested with the protection and advancement
      of mankind, if you take her late Merethic, early First era behavior into account.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 17d7fb6524a48624b8f800e8b355e0ad, type: 2}
    dialog: I'm... not sure I've heard anyone speak of eras before the Third before...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Like I said, Skyrim really isn't a place for proper academia.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: The best you get is a school for magic, which has blatant survival purposes,
      and a school for music, to glorify deeds for history.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Anyway, can you teach me those words now that you know my intentions,
      or not?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 17d7fb6524a48624b8f800e8b355e0ad, type: 2}
    dialog: Very well, I show give you my knowledge of those words, and we shall
      see if your plan will come to fruition.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 'A gust of wind bursts from Arngeir, as he bestows upon me the knowledge
      of three words:'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: <font=dragonfont>lingr4, v1l, tinv1k.</font>
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Long, distance, communication...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267988772749426
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 17d7fb6524a48624b8f800e8b355e0ad, type: 2}
    dialog: Go on. Let the meanings of the words flow through you, meditate on their,
      and your, purpose.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267988772749427
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I think about what I'm trying to do.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I think about what the words mean.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I think.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I think...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I speak.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: <font=dragonfont>lingr4 v1l tinv1k</font>!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267988772749428
    - rid: 4972360390599770178
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4351267988772749429
    - rid: 4351267988772749431
    - rid: 4351267988772749432
    - rid: 4351267988772749433
